"`state=running`+`ota_validated=true`), dedicated "
"`Ready/ClockUnsynced` condition, `LastHeartbeat` still updated (no "
"silence, §2)"

#: ../../liaison/tracabilite.md
msgid ""
"✔ (2026-07-27) `main/embewi_heartbeat.c:177` émet "
"`reason:\"clock_unsynced\"` tant que `!embewi_time_is_set()` ; `:106-110`"
" bascule `emit_to()` sur `embewi_tls_relaxed_post()` (nouveau fichier "
"`main/embewi_tls_relaxed.c`) — mbedTLS bas niveau, "
"`MBEDTLS_SSL_VERIFY_OPTIONAL` + inspection manuelle post-handshake : "
"seuls `BADCERT_EXPIRED`/`BADCERT_FUTURE` tolérés, chaîne/CN restent "
"bloquants (`embewi_ssl_get_verify_result`). Nécessaire car "
"`esp_http_client`/esp-tls force `VERIFY_REQUIRED` dès qu'une CA est "
"configurée, sans hook pour ne relâcher que la date. Contrepartie : "
"`CONFIG_MBEDTLS_HAVE_TIME_DATE=y` activé en prod "
"(`sdkconfig.defaults.prod:57`) — **écart pré-existant découvert pendant "
"l'implémentation** : cette vérif était jusque-là silencieusement "
"désactivée dans TOUS les états (comportement par défaut ESP-IDF), donc la"
" vérification stricte post-synchro n'existait pas non plus avant ce "
"correctif. **Portée limitée, assumée** : le canal de détresse couvre le "
"heartbeat et `embewi_log_emit()` (events OTA/lifecycle via HTTPS, tous "
"deux via `emit_to()`) mais **pas** le streaming `ESP_LOGx` → WebSocket "
"(`embewi_log.c`, `esp_websocket_client`) — pas de hook `VERIFY_OPTIONAL` "
"équivalent côté client WS, et ce flux est déjà best-effort/lossy par "
"conception (cf. commentaire en tête de `embewi_log.c`). Le heartbeat (§2,"
" jamais silencieux) est garanti ; ce flux logs, non, pendant la fenêtre "
"`clock_unsynced`"
msgstr ""
"✔ (2026-07-27) `main/embewi_heartbeat.c:177` emits "
"`reason:\"clock_unsynced\"` while `!embewi_time_is_set()`; `:106-110` "
"switches `emit_to()` over to `embewi_tls_relaxed_post()` (new file "
"`main/embewi_tls_relaxed.c`) — low-level mbedTLS, "
"`MBEDTLS_SSL_VERIFY_OPTIONAL` + manual post-handshake inspection: only "
"`BADCERT_EXPIRED`/`BADCERT_FUTURE` tolerated, chain/CN remain blocking "
"(`embewi_ssl_get_verify_result`). Necessary because "
"`esp_http_client`/esp-tls forces `VERIFY_REQUIRED` as soon as a CA is "
"configured, with no hook to relax only the date check. Trade-off: "
"`CONFIG_MBEDTLS_HAVE_TIME_DATE=y` enabled in production "
"(`sdkconfig.defaults.prod:57`) — **pre-existing gap discovered during "
"implementation**: this check was until then silently disabled in ALL "
"states (default ESP-IDF behavior), so the strict post-sync check "
"didn't exist before this fix either. **Deliberately limited scope**: "
"the distress channel covers the heartbeat and `embewi_log_emit()` "
"(OTA/lifecycle events via HTTPS, both through `emit_to()`) but **not**"
" `ESP_LOGx` → WebSocket streaming (`embewi_log.c`, "
"`esp_websocket_client`) — no equivalent `VERIFY_OPTIONAL` hook on the "
"WS client side, and this flow is already best-effort/lossy by design "
"(see the comment at the top of `embewi_log.c`). The heartbeat (§2, "
"never silent) is guaranteed; this log flow isn't, during the "
"`clock_unsynced` window"

